**Goal Model – Food Delivery in a Hospital**

| Goal ID | Goal Title                     | Text                                                                                                 | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type | Relation |
|---------|--------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|---------------------|-----------|----------|
| G1      | Deliver Food to Inpatient Room | Ensure that the ordered meal(s) are successfully delivered to the patient’s room.                 | ; (sequential)     | Perform   | –        |
| G2      | Obtain Delivery Order          | Query the kitchen system for the next order to be fulfilled.                                         | -                   | Query     | AND      |
| G3      | Retrieve Meal(s) from Kitchen   | Pick up the ordered meal(s) from the kitchen area.                                                   | -                   | Perform   | AND      |
| G4      | Determine Retrieval Capability  | Check the patient record and room‑presence data to decide if the patient can fetch the meal from the tray. | -                   | Query     | AND      |
| G5      | Deliver Food to Patient         | Execute the chosen delivery method (table or hand‑over).                                            | FALLBACK(G5.1,G5.2) | Perform   | AND      |
| G5.1    | Deliver to Table                | Place the meal on the patient’s table using the robot’s manipulation skill.                           | -                   | Perform   | –        |
| G5.2    | Hand Over to Patient           | Give the meal to the patient (or companion/nurse/robot) and confirm correct retrieval.              | -                   | Perform   | –        |
| G6      | Retrieve Dirty Dishes          | Pick up all dirty dishes from the patient’s room.                                                     | -                   | Perform   | AND      |
| G7      | Open Room Door                 | Open the patient room door, possibly with assistance from another robot or a human.                 | -                   | Perform   | AND      |

