### Tasks

| Task ID | Task Title                     | Text                                                                                                 | Relation | Location          | Number of Robots | Justification |
|---------|--------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|----------|-------------------|------------------|---------------|
| AT0     | Query Kitchen System           | Ask the kitchen system for the next order to be processed.                                            | AND      | Kitchen System    | 1                | Only one robot needs to query the system. |
| AT1     | Navigate to Kitchen Pickup    | Move from current location to the kitchen pickup area.                                                 | AND      | Kitchen           | 1                | Robot must physically reach the kitchen. |
| AT2     | Pick Up Meal(s)                | Use manipulation skill to lift and secure the meal(s) in the robot’s tray.                              | AND      | Kitchen           | 1                | Single robot handles the meal. |
| AT3     | Query Inpatient Record         | Retrieve patient record and companion presence data to assess retrieval capability.                     | AND      | System            | 1                | Robot queries a database; no physical movement required. |
| AT4     | Deliver to Table               | Place the meal on the patient’s table using the robot’s manipulation skill.                            | AND      | Inpatient Room    | 1                | Direct action in the room. |
| AT5     | Hand Over Meal to Patient       | Pass the meal to the patient (or companion/nurse/robot).                                               | AND      | Inpatient Room    | 1                | Robot must be present in the room. |
| AT6     | Indicate Meal ID to Patient    | Communicate which meal the patient should retrieve (if multiple meals are carried).                    | AND      | Inpatient Room    | 1                | Robot needs to inform the patient. |
| AT7     | Track Retrieval Time/Location  | Log the timestamp and location when the patient retrieves the meal.                                    | AND      | Inpatient Room    | 1                | Robot must monitor retrieval. |
| AT8     | Alert Wrong Meal Retrieved     | Notify staff if the patient picks up an incorrect meal.                                               | AND      | Inpatient Room    | 1                | Robot must detect mismatch. |
| AT9     | Retrieve Dirty Dishes          | Pick up all dirty dishes from the room, possibly with another robot or a human.                       | AND      | Inpatient Room    | [1,2]            | Dish retrieval may require cooperation; range allows one or two robots. |
| AT10    | Open Room Door                 | Open the patient room door, optionally requesting human assistance if needed.                         | AND      | Room Door         | [1,2]            | Door opening may need another robot or a human; range allows cooperation. |

